From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: an Electron app's page loads its handled schemes

An Electron app window's page loads file: and the app's own schemes from
the app, and its http and https requests go to the app first when its
session handles them, as Electron's protocol.handle does.

ChromeContentBrowserClient hands an Electron page's navigations and
subresources in those schemes to the app's loader, replacing content's
file: loader there, and puts the app in front of the page's network
loads. A guest navigates only to web-safe schemes, so content asks the
embedder, through ContentBrowserClient::MayGuestLoadUnsafeScheme, whether
this guest may load a scheme that is not. See
chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_electron_loader.h.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
